{"id":"eber","name":"Eber","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:eber"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Eber","text":"Beyond. (1.). The third post-duluvian patriach after Shem (Gen. 10:24; 11:14). He is regarded as the founder of the Hebrew race (10:21; Num. 24:24). In Luke 3:35 he is called Heber. (2.) One of the seven heads of the families of the Gadites (1 Chr. 5:13). (3.) The oldest of the three sons of Elpaal the Benjamite (8:12). (4.) One of the heads of the familes of Benjamites in Jerusalem (22). (5.) The head of the priestly family of Amok in the time of Zerubbabel (Neh. 12:20)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H5677","lemma":"עֵבֵר","xlit":"ʻÊbêr","gloss":"Eber, the name of two patriarchs and four Israelites","kjv":"Eber, Heber","count":11,"share":0.79},{"strong":"H3205","lemma":"יָלַד","xlit":"yâlad","gloss":"to bear young","kjv":"bear, beget, birth, born","count":5,"share":0.36},{"strong":"H251","lemma":"אָח","xlit":"ʼâch","gloss":"a brother )","kjv":"another, brother; kindred, like, other","count":4,"share":0.29},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":6,"share":0.43}],"verses":["Gen.10.21","Gen.10.24","Gen.10.25","Gen.11.14","Num.24.24","1Chr.1.19","1Chr.1.25","1Chr.5.13","1Chr.8.12","1Chr.8.22","Neh.12.20","Gen.10.22","Gen.10.23","Luke.3.35"],"related":[{"id":"peleg","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.167,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"salah","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.158,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"heber","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.125,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"shem","type":"cooccur","shared":8,"jaccard":0.092,"why":"8 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"sciences","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.06,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"genealogy","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.02,"why":"4 verses are indexed u